															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-cimmerian" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1414765); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1414765&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607460370" alt="Doctor Cimmerian" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1414765)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-cimmerian" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1414765); return false;" >Doctor Cimmerian</a></span> <span class="odate time_1514867901 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Jan 2018 04:38</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3671673">
									

<p>Aha! It has arrived! This was a lot of fun to work on and I'm very satisfied with how it came out.</p>
<p>Credits:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The two pieces of artwork here and on the supplement were created by Zhange.</p>
<p>The two photographs of divers are from these sources: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RMS_Rhone_2003_8.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RMS_Rhone_2003_8.jpg</a> and <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Divers_in_wheelhouse_2.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Divers_in_wheelhouse_2.jpg</a> .</p>
<p>The remaining images were created by djkaktus.</p>
<p>The audio was created as a joint effort between myself and TheVolgun. I play the part of the monster/Nereus, and TheVolgun plays the part of Setrate. Audio editing was done by me, and the following sound effects were layered in as part of that process:</p>
<p>Metal Breaking Apart:<br />
<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x5qw1rWxssI">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x5qw1rWxssI</a> From the royalty free youtube audio library.<br />
Rusty Gears:<br />
<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k1l-E2UyyRY">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k1l-E2UyyRY</a> With reuse allowed by the creator.<br />
Water Dripping:<br />
<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cyQos90QNCU">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cyQos90QNCU</a> Which is licensed creative commons.</p>
<p>I think that's everything, but I may update this if I missed anything.</p>
<p>You know, I always assumed that quote about &quot;the men who felled Hyperion&quot; would be an obvious historical reference but it's lifted from Appian of Alexandria if anyone missed that.</p>
</div>
</div>
